# Copy to .env.mockup.local (git-ignored). The data of the mockup (Datasource + Storage) lives ONLY on the file server every developer shares
# (D:\mockup-data on the Docker host, behind https): `npm run mockup` starts the dev server and sends /mockup-api there. There is no local copy.
MOCKUP_REMOTE_URL=https://acedemo.acecloud.co.th:7339
# the shared secret of the server: ask whoever runs it (it is in .env.mockup-server on the Docker host)
MOCKUP_TOKEN=
# MOCKUP_WORKSPACE=<your name>   OPTIONAL. Leave it out and you share the ONE state with everybody (what anybody does is seen by all at once). Set it to try things
#                                 without touching the data of the others: what you write goes to Datasource/_workspaces/<name>/ on the server and only you see it.
# Which address to connect to instead of looking the domain up (the name stays in https + Host, so the certificate is still checked):
#   - on the machine that RUNS the gateway (acedemo): its own public address does not come back to it  ->  MOCKUP_REMOTE_IP=127.0.0.1
#   - on every OTHER machine of the office network: the domain points to the public address, where this port may not be open yet
#       ->  MOCKUP_REMOTE_IP=192.168.24.233   (the LAN address of the acedemo machine)
#   - from outside the office: leave it empty (needs the port forwarded by infra)
# Do NOT copy the 127.0.0.1 of the acedemo machine to another one: it then connects to ITSELF and every call fails (ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1).
# MOCKUP_REMOTE_IP=192.168.24.233
